ry  throwing a super slow punch it's  interesting train for the traits as well  as the skills if you want to learn to  handstand for instance you need to  shoulder mobility core strength shoulder  strength prefer ception and more these  things can be trained separately and  they'll greatly shorten your time to  master the skill and keep learning the  more you learn the more BDNF and  dopamine your brain produces increasing  plasticity theoretically learning a new  skill could even help you to progress  faster with your regular lifts by  helping you to gain more neural Drive of  course you probably are not Batman  therefore you likely don't need to be an  expert stunt driver and to know every  martial art but if you apply these  strategies then you may be able to  progress more quickly than you think in  more areas than you imagined and I'd  love to know any strategies you've used  in the comments down below if you like  this kind of training then check out the  link in the description down below to  find my ebook and training program super  functional training down there you'll  also find a link to the written article  version of this post where I include all  references etc a huge shout out and  thanks to all my patrons who helped me  over at patreon calm if you'd like to  learn more about that then that link is  also down there it really does make a  huge difference  hit subscribe if you want more like this  or take a look around the blog and of  course I'll see you next time thanks a  ton for watching and bye for now

